Actually, a cleaner standard approach for this game: sample the segment at intervals no greater than min(BRICK_H, BRICK_W) or so. Let me implement:

```js
function sweptCollision(ball, brick, px, py) {
  const dx = ball.x - px;
  const dy = ball.y - py;
  const dist = Math.hypot(dx, dy);
  const steps = Math.max(1, Math.ceil(dist / (BALL_R))); // sample every ≤ r px
